\contentsline {table}{\numberline {6.1}{\ignorespaces Comparison of the considered integration methods properties.}}{61}{table.caption.41}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {6.2}{\ignorespaces Statistics of the controlled 3D pendulum for desired rotations about the $x$-axis. The terminal error is defined as $e_R(T)=\lVert R_N-R_{\mathrm {des}}\rVert _F$. The manifold violation is $\max _k\varepsilon _{R,k}$ with $\varepsilon _{R,k}=\lVert R_k^\top R_k-I_3\rVert _F$. The rank metric $\delta _{\max }$ follows Teng's definition $\delta _k=|\lambda _{k,2}|/|\lambda _{k,1}|$, computed over the actual sub-moment matrices used for trajectory extraction. The trajectory quantities are evaluated using the ordered extraction, and the reported runtime is the MOSEK optimizer time.}}{74}{table.caption.53}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {6.3}{\ignorespaces Statistics of the Acrobot trajectory optimization using the \textbf {Full SELF} sparsity setting (complete stage-wise cliques $I_k$) for desired absolute rotations of both links. The terminal rotation error is defined as $e_R(T) = \left ( \DOTSB \sum@ \slimits@ _{i=1}^{2} \left \|R_{i,N}-R_{i,\mathrm {des}}\right \|_F^2 \right )^{1/2}$. The maximum manifold violation is $\varepsilon _{\mathrm {SO(2)}}^{\max } = \max _{i,k,X\in \{R,F\}} \|X_{i,k}^{\top }X_{i,k}-I_2\|_F$. For each moment block $j$, $\delta _j$ denotes Teng's rank ratio $\delta _j=|\lambda _{j,2}|/|\lambda _{j,1}|$, where the eigenvalues are sorted by magnitude. Thus, $\delta _{\max }=\max _j\delta _j$, while $\delta _{\mathrm {first}}$ is evaluated for the first moment block. All trajectory metrics use the ordered extraction, and the runtime is the solver operation time.}}{76}{table.caption.56}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {6.4}{\ignorespaces Statistics of the Acrobot trajectory optimization using the \textbf {Hybrid SELF} sparsity setting, which preserves the first two full cliques and separates the later dynamics and kinematic constraints, for desired absolute rotations of both links. All metrics ($e_R(T)$, $\varepsilon _{\mathrm {SO(2)}}^{\max }$, $\delta _{\max }$, $\delta _{\mathrm {first}}$, and runtime) are defined as in Table~\ref {tab:acrobot_sdp_statistics_full}.}}{76}{table.caption.57}%
